{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/973363-has-anyone-use-hunting-ground-the-rockies-in-2e","id":973363,"title":"Has anyone use Hunting Ground: The Rockies in 2E?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-20T13:49:13-07:00","id":973363,"title":"Has anyone use Hunting Ground: The Rockies in 2E?","content":"Hello everyone, so im preparing to run a Werewolf campaign and im impressed how good the city book (Region book?) for Denver is. While other city books always go special snoflakey and out-of-the-box without establishing the box first, this one is as vanilla as it can with every single element of werewolf there to showcase to new players.<br /> <br /> im wondering has anyone used the setting in 2E? Considering the changes from 1st edition to second there are a few things that could and some that should change.<br /> <br /> Stats aside has anyone keeps the packs as they are? Or have you transformed/introduce wolfblooded packmates to the city packs? Considering the now massive size of packs in 2nd (6 to 10 packmates*) edition comparing from 1 (3 to 5 packmates).<br /> <br /> And the main conflict does it really hold water in 2e? The whole angle of multitribal pack with Max Roman vs Unitribal packs with Rachel Snow seems off. Maybe it was a holdover from Apocalypse (as they are a quite a few Apocalypses typos in the book) but in 1st edition tribe seems meaningless and multitribal packs seem the norm more than the exception.<br /> <br /> And now with 2e new focus on sacred prey more even unitribal packs seems like a very heavy handicap considering everysingle enemy is a plenty on Denver.<br /> <br /> I could see modifying Roman motivation from &quot;multitribal&quot; pack to a protectorate or a &quot;Uratha nation&quot; but Rachel snow seems incredible contrary if one applies 2nd.<br /> <br /> So im curious those using Denver, what have you done? Have you make any of the sides (Roman vs Snow) the right one? <br /> <br /> *meaning 3 with at least a wolfblooded for a minimun of 6 packmates to 10)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T14:46:17-07:00","id":973400,"title":"","content":"I had plans to run this setting for 2e, but it never got off the ground. I was planning to set the game in 2007, because that was the year the book was published, and a lot of things were kind of tied to the time. For example, the whole multi-tribal vs. single-tribe packs thing, while probably an Apocalypse holdover, was also directly tied into the whole &quot;the brethren war just ended&quot; thing that Forsaken had going on in the early years. Almost 10 years later, I'm not sure if the brethren war just having ended really works as well any more. Another big thing is, so much of the book is built around the idea that Gurdilag's defeat was relatively recent. With each passing year getting further from the Apollo missions, the longer Gurdilag must have been wrecking Denver's spiritscape if its defeat was so recent.<br /> <br /> So, the way I saw it, there are basically two ways to go about bringing Hunting Ground: the Rockies into 2e - either as direct a conversion as possible, set in the mid-late aughts, or to advance the story, metaplot-style along with the mechanics. I decided to go with the former, since I thought it would be less work, but the latter could potentially be more interesting. There are a few things that were set up to be right on the cusp of change - Lillian and Ezikiel's baby is 8 or 9 by now. Morrison has either broken the Pickering family curse or died. Kim Carlson is likely coming into her own as a Bone Shadow. Josie Raincaller is definitely dead by now, and without her to keep the peace, the tension between Iron Soul and Sky's First Defender will likely have come to a head, possibly breaking up the Mountain's Proud Children, which could be a <i>huge </i>deal if it left Sakendar Isi undefended. There's no way Shadow of Smoke and Fire is still together. Andrea Waters has probably gotten up to big things since joining the Silver Syndicate. I wouldn't be surprised if Jagged Sky's pack has broken up. I'm sure New Hope would have found a Totem by now, but Nikki's Totem-mandated five years in a blessed pack is long since passed, so she may have left to go back to her old pack. That would leave New Hope in an awkward spot, being the supposed model of Max Roman's dreams, if their Storm Lord left the pack, where does that leave them? Crash was hinted to be on the cusp of leaving Echoes of Thunder, that may or may not have happened by now. And then there's the Su'Ur pack. Did they succeed in strengthening Gurdilag's memory to the point where it might be able to re-form?<br /> <br /> There's also some question of whether or not the characters should remain the same Tribes that they were originally written as. The Scar Angels, for instance, were written as Blood Talons, presumably because Blood Talons were the warrior tribe in 1e and they've got a whole road warrior thing going on. But, they would also make a perfect fit for the Thousand Steel Teeth, which is an Iron Master Lodge. The Echoes of Thunder were Storm Lords, I think mostly because they were the leader tribe in 1e, but with Rachel's focus on Uratha strengthening themselves by way of internal conflict, and wishing the brethren war hadn't ended because fighting each other made them stronger, she should really be a Blood Talon in 2e's paradigm, and you could make a good case for most if not all of her pack to do the same. Black Moon Extreme, with their focus on hunting vampires are an interesting case because they <i>have a Sacred Prey</i>. In 2e, they would probably be members of a Lodge, or trying to start a new Lodge, with vampires as their Sacred Prey. On a similar note, the Red Knives were doing the whole Wolf-Blooded and human packmates thing even back then. They can just slot into 2e pretty much exactly as-written.<br /> <br /> Quick note on geography: the book has the Three Sisters set up in a bookstore on the Pearl Street Pedestrian Mall, which it claims is in Denver. It's not, it's in Boulder. But, that could be kind of cool, with all the stuff Muthsaga the Smiling One and the Blissful Friends Network were up to there, to see how they would get involved in all that. Also, if Muthsaga is still around, I could see it being <i>veeeeeerry </i>happy with the legalization of marajuana in Colorado. Especially in a Boulder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T19:30:33-07:00","id":974820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/973363-has-anyone-use-hunting-ground-the-rockies-in-2e?p=973400#post973400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also some question of whether or not the characters should remain the same Tribes that they were originally written as. The Scar Angels, for instance, were written as Blood Talons, presumably because Blood Talons were the warrior tribe in 1e and they've got a whole road warrior thing going on. But, they would also make a perfect fit for the Thousand Steel Teeth, which is an Iron Master Lodge. The Echoes of Thunder were Storm Lords, I think mostly because they were the leader tribe in 1e, but with Rachel's focus on Uratha strengthening themselves by way of internal conflict, and wishing the brethren war hadn't ended because fighting each other made them stronger, she should really be a Blood Talon in 2e's paradigm, and you could make a good case for most if not all of her pack to do the same. Black Moon Extreme, with their focus on hunting vampires are an interesting case because they <i>have a Sacred Prey</i>. In 2e, they would probably be members of a Lodge, or trying to start a new Lodge, with vampires as their Sacred Prey. On a similar note, the Red Knives were doing the whole Wolf-Blooded and human packmates thing even back then. They can just slot into 2e pretty much exactly as-written.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the 1000 steel teeth Iron master only? But aside from that yeah the Scar angels are gonna be straight up Thousand Steel Lodge members.<br /> <br /> As for Rachel Snow that more difficult to answer for me. For one i like the idea of Storm Lords vs Iron Masters and while is true she thinks pack should fight each other for strenghtening i dont seer her choosing Uratha as her prey more as she doesnt wanna kill other uratha but just remain in the current system. Personally im leaning on her view as the Protectorate as something temporal Vs Roman idea of as something permanent.<br /> <br /> Black Moon extreme, i think is gonna remain a illfitted Storm lord pack. They are written as harmless idiot antagonist and the idea of this pack of posers that even Rachel snow dont wanna be associated with is kinda funny.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/973363-has-anyone-use-hunting-ground-the-rockies-in-2e?p=973400#post973400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick note on geography: the book has the Three Sisters set up in a bookstore on the Pearl Street Pedestrian Mall, which it claims is in Denver. It's not, it's in Boulder. But, that could be kind of cool, with all the stuff Muthsaga the Smiling One and the Blissful Friends Network were up to there, to see how they would get involved in all that. Also, if Muthsaga is still around, I could see it being <i>veeeeeerry </i>happy with the legalization of marajuana in Colorado. Especially in a Boulder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T20:09:33-07:00","id":974839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/973363-has-anyone-use-hunting-ground-the-rockies-in-2e?p=974820#post974820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the 1000 steel teeth Iron master only? But aside from that yeah the Scar angels are gonna be straight up Thousand Steel Lodge members.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only, but predominantly. Even the Screaming Moon Lodge is only primarily Cahalith, not only.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Rachel Snow that more difficult to answer for me. For one i like the idea of Storm Lords vs Iron Masters and while is true she thinks pack should fight each other for strenghtening i dont seer her choosing Uratha as her prey more as she doesnt wanna kill other uratha but just remain in the current system. Personally im leaning on her view as the Protectorate as something temporal Vs Roman idea of as something permanent. </div> </div> </div>That seems like an easy conversion. Roman is pro-Protectorate. Working together we can be stronger, if another threat arises we can all deal with it and not have it slowly pick off pack by pack with no one noticing because we don't keep in touch. And Snow, fitting her strong Storm Lord nature and legacy, believes such a thing would weaken the packs. How could werewolves grow strong against threats, if they knew another pack would come save them? She could even point at Roman himself as an example. He practically single-handedly sought out the bane of the idigam and defeated it, and now he's one of the most powerful werewolves in the Rockies.<br /> <br /> Neither idea is a bad one, really. The idea of a protectorate is a great one. The reality is that it's so hard it's rarely worked in the long-term. But just because it's hard doesn't mean it's not worth doing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Black Moon extreme, i think is gonna remain a illfitted Storm lord pack. They are written as harmless idiot antagonist and the idea of this pack of posers that even Rachel snow dont wanna be associated with is kinda funny. </div> </div> </div>Read the intro fiction. It follows Moriarty, who knows what a lousy place they're in. He wants to be more. And someone's there to give him what he wants.<br /> <br /> I used a little bit of the Rockies, only Red Snow's pack. A game I played had a few different packs from it, including Rachel Snow's. Nothing in second edition, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-25T11:46:28-07:00","id":976032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/973363-has-anyone-use-hunting-ground-the-rockies-in-2e?p=974839#post974839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used a little bit of the Rockies, only Red Snow's pack. A game I played had a few different packs from it, including Rachel Snow's. Nothing in second edition, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, im thinking of introduce them as the poser pack and showing an fake improvement on moriarty side (product of him getting lunar gifts from mad lunes).<br /> <br /> I found a piece of fiction centered in denver at the start of the Rage is there any other fiction based on Denver?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}